    (uuid bd82d116-e441-4223-9528-800be498e98a)
  )

  (text "USB-C connector subsystem (pilink-7el.7). Device-only (UFP) wiring, rear-exit\nplacement per the user's requirement that the cable run straight back out of the\nenclosure. USB 2.0 only -- RP2350B has no USB3 PHY -- so no CC logic/PD chip is\nneeded, just passive 5.1k pulldowns on CC1/CC2 (Rd, advertising \"sink, default\nUSB power\" per the USB-C spec).\n\nJ401: LCSC C7463258 (TYPE-C-31-D-09, mfr Hroparts/HRO), a vertical-mount,\nthrough-hole 16-pin USB-C receptacle -- swapped from the original horizontal\nSMD TYPE-C-31-M-12 in pilink-7el.11, per the upright-desk-clock form factor\ndecision (.planning/decisions/2026-11-15-upright-desk-clock-form-factor.md):\nthe PCB stands parallel to the enclosure's front face, so the rear-exit USB-C\nconnector's mating axis must run perpendicular to the PCB, which this M-12's\nhorizontal edge-mount body cannot do. Part selected and researched in\npilink-0do (.research/findings/2026-11-15-vertical-usb-c-receptacle-selection.md);\nlive stock 5,651 units at swap time (2026-11-15, JLCPCB's public API --\nthe jlcpcb-search MCP tool's own local-database snapshot reads 5,490, a known\nstale-cache gap flagged in that finding; recheck again before ordering),\nExtended-library part (standard extended-part handling fee, not a\nsourcing-availability risk). Pinout is IDENTICAL to the part it replaces --\nverified directly from TYPE-C-31-D-09's own datasheet table (fetched and read\ndirectly, 2026-11-15) against KiCad's stock Connector:USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0_16P\nsymbol already used here -- an exact match, including the A1/A12/B1/B12 GND and\nA4/A9/B4/B9 VBUS pins, which the stock symbol already stacks onto one visible pin\neach (hidden duplicate pin numbers at the same graphical point), so a single wire\nto that point ties all 4 physical pins together internally -- no manual tying\nneeded for GND/VBUS, only for the two D+/D- pairs below. This bead's swap is\nFOOTPRINT-ONLY: no symbol/pin/net change, R401-R404's CC-sense wiring (below)\nis untouched. Footprint: hand-authored\nConnector_USB_Custom:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-D-09 (no stock KiCad\nfootprint matches this exact manufacturer part; see that footprint's own descr\nfor the full datasheet-dimension sourcing. The shell/peg slots' X offset was\noriginally mis-measured as ~3.30mm (PR #41 review caught it) and is now\ncorrected to +-2.50mm, independently re-verified against the datasheet's own\nPCB-layout-recommendation drawing's 5.00mm slot-centerline-spacing dimension --\nthe ~3.30mm figure was a real datasheet dimension but for the A5/A8 signal-pad\nspan, not a slot offset. No dimension from this footprint remains flagged as\nneeding a further human cross-check before fab, though the standard\nhand-authored-footprint visual/placement GUI review still applies). Mounting: genuine\nthrough-hole shell pegs (not SMT tabs), 6.50mm body height above the PCB,\nmounted on the PCB's BACK side per the form-factor decision -- actual PCB\nplacement/back-side mounting is pilink-7el.12's job, out of scope here.\nAssembly: per pilink-0do's recommendation, JLCPCB double-sided PCBA (not\nhand-soldering) given the repeated mechanical plug-insertion/removal load this\nconnector's joints have to survive -- see hardware/BOM.md's J401 row and\nassembly-flag note.\n\nDP1/DP2 (A6/B6, both datasheet-labeled D+) are tied together and routed to the\nUSB_DP global label; DN1/DN2 (A7/B7, both D-) are tied together and routed to\nUSB_DM. Both global labels are reused exactly as already declared in\nrp2350b_memory.kicad_sch (confirmed via grep before use, same case/text) --\nRP2350B's own USB PHY handles the shorted-together pairs fine at USB2 speeds;\nthis is the standard low-cost pattern for a connector that exposes both plug\norientations' D+/D- separately, not a hack. SBU1/SBU2 (A8/B8) are left\nunconnected (no_connect flags) -- no DisplayPort/Thunderbolt alt-mode in this\ndesign. The SHIELD pin (S1, the connector's metal shell/mounting-tab contacts --\nnot part of the USB-C spec's 16 signal/power pins, and not mentioned in the\noriginal pin-table investigation) is tied directly to GND, the standard\nchassis-to-signal-ground tie used by most USB-C reference designs for a\nsingle-ground-plane board like this one.\n" (at 20 20 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a00ebf83-9056-4b8e-9e59-0b66b52db85d)
  )

  (text "F401: VBUS overcurrent\nprotection, sized properly per\npilink-imx after the first\nattempt (C269104, 500mA hold) was\nremoved on review for being\nundersized. Chosen: LCSC C269106\n(Brightking SMD0805B100TFT), an\n0805 PTC resettable fuse, 1A hold\n/ 1.95A trip / 6V max /\nR@25C=40mOhm (initial, 25C),\n5,460 units in stock at research\ntime -- lower than its siblings\nbut not zero, worth rechecking at\norder time. In series between the\nconnector's VBUS and the +5V net\npower.kicad_sch expects from this\nsheet, same position the earlier,\nremoved attempt used.\n\nSizing: worst-case peak current\n(not steady -- see\npower.kicad_sch's U1 note for the\nfull budget derivation)\nre-derived from power.kicad_sch's\nown budget (RP2350B tens of mA +\nESP32-WROOM-32U up to 500mA per\nEspressif's TX-burst spec +\ndisplay ~50-100mA incl." (at 20 156 0)
    (effects (font (size 0.9 0.9)) (justify left top))
    (uuid baa5b7eb-3373-4ba6-b52c-85928e3005b5)
  )
  (text "backlight) = ~0.6-0.65A. Picked\nthe 1A hold variant (C269106)\nover the 750mA sibling (C269105,\nR@25C=90mOhm) because 0.65A is\n65% of a 1A hold rating vs 87% of\na 750mA rating -- 65% leaves\nheadroom for the\nambient-temperature hold-current\nderating all PTC fuses exhibit\nonce enclosed (this family's own\nderating curve is a scanned,\nnon-text-extractable image in its\ndatasheet, so this uses the\ngeneral <=75-80%-of-rated\nguideline for this part class as\na flagged assumption, not read\noff this datasheet's own curve).\n\nSeries-resistance-vs-dropout\ncheck: this part's LCSC/JLCPCB\nlisting gives both an initial\nR@25C=40mOhm and an R1(max)\npost-trip resistance of 230mOhm\n-- the resistance that actually\napplies after any trip event or\nunder worse-case conditions, not\njust at first power-up. At the\n0.65A worst case that's a 26mV" (at 59 156 0)
    (effects (font (size 0.9 0.9)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 904498bc-05a6-4a9a-8ddb-b110a7a731c0)
  )
  (text "(40mOhm) to 150mV (230mOhm) added\ndrop, not a flat 26mV. Negligible\nis a reasonable claim at the\n40mOhm end but less so at the\n230mOhm end, against U1's\n(AP2114H-3.3)\ndropout-vs-VBUS-floor margin --\nresolved per power.kicad_sch's\nown U1 note (pilink-ddq), whose\nmargin math already folds in both\nof this fuse's resistance cases\n(26mV normal / 150mV post-trip),\nso no separate correction is\nneeded here.\n\nR401/R402: 5.1k ohm Rd pulldowns\non CC1/CC2 to GND,\nResistor_SMD:R_0402_1005Metric\n(same footprint convention as the\nother pull resistors in this\nproject, e.g. input.kicad_sch's\nA/B/X/Y pull-ups). 5.1k is the\nUSB-C spec's standard sink-side\nRd value, not a project-specific\nchoice.\n\nReferences use a new 400-499\nblock for this sheet" (at 98 156 0)
    (effects (font (size 0.9 0.9)) (justify left top))
    (uuid fdb81270-ca05-4d97-afa1-887bbabf98c6)
  )
  (text "(power.kicad_sch: 1-99,\nrp2350b_memory.kicad_sch:\n100-199, esp32_bt.kicad_sch:\n200-299, input.kicad_sch:\n300-399) -- J401, F401,\nR401-R404, #PWR401-#PWR405.\ndisplay.kicad_sch took the\nplanned 500-599 block when\npilink-7el.5 populated it.\n\nNo PWR_FLAG is added on this\nsheet's +5V or GND nets:\npower.kicad_sch already carries\nboth (#FLG01 on +5V, #FLG02 on\nGND), satisfying ERC project-wide\nfor those two nets regardless of\nwhat drives them downstream. The\nUSB-C connector's own VBUS/GND\npins are \"passive\"-type pins (not\n\"power_out\"), so wiring them into\n+5V/GND here does not create a\nsecond driver or an ERC\n\"conflicting power outputs\" error\n-- same reasoning already\ndocumented on esp32_bt.kicad_sch\nfor why a local PWR_FLAG should\nNOT be added once a real upstream\ndriver/flag exists." (at 137 156 0)
    (effects (font (size 0.9 0.9)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 658f5293-ffdc-4147-9a83-baed4ca9f958)
  )

