    (uuid bfef93fa-28c1-4ccd-bf11-03259ea16fcd)
  )

  (text "R403/R404, CC1/CC2 voltage-sense tap (pilink-1sj): 10k series-protection\nresistors (not a divider -- RP2350B's ADC input draws no DC current while\nsampling once firmware disables that pin's default pull-down and input\nbuffer per the RP2350-E9 erratum, so these don't perturb the R401/R402 Rd\npulldown voltage they tap; they exist only to limit fault current into the\nGPIO's ESD clamp if a non-compliant source drives CC above its normal\n<=3.3V-ish range). Routed to GPIO40_ADC0/GPIO41_ADC1\n(rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch U101 pins 49/52) -- both previously-unused\nADC-capable GPIOs (GPIO47_ADC7 is already taken, repurposed as the PSRAM's\nsecond QMI chip-select). Both CC lines are sensed, not just one: a Type-C\nreceptacle's Rp (source current advertisement) lands on whichever of\nCC1/CC2 the cable orientation connects -- the other reads ~0V through its\nown idle Rd -- so sensing only one would misread \"no advertisement\" on\nevery other cable flip.\n\nWhat this tap actually buys (corrected from this bead's first-pass note,\nwhich wrongly said this only matters if BC1.2/PD hardware is added later):\nUSB-C's 1.5A/3A current-advertisement tiers are set purely by the host's\nRp value and read directly off CC voltage -- independent of USB data\nspeed. Only the Default tier (500mA vs 900mA) depends on USB generation.\nSo this tap lets firmware legitimately draw the ~0.65A worst-case peak\n(power.kicad_sch's U1 note, this sheet's F401 note) TODAY on any host\nwhose Rp advertises 1.5A or 3A -- a common tier for real Type-C host\nports per TI's TUSB320/321 current-mode datasheets -- with no BC1.2/PD\nhardware needed. On a host that only advertises Default (500mA), this\ndevice still only has a 500mA entitlement; firmware should throttle its\nreal peak (e.g. don't let ESP32 TX-burst and max backlight coincide)\nspecifically when Default is sensed. That firmware logic is out of this\nrepo's scope. Full analysis and the correction itself:\n.research/findings/2026-11-15-usb-c-default-power-compliance.md, pilink-1sj." (at 170 15 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid d4e5f6a7-8b9c-4012-a345-6b7c8d9e0f1a)
  )

